  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / <a href="/gear">Gear</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech">Budget tech</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech/compare">Compare</a> / Sennheiser Momentum 4 vs Soundcore Q30</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">Head to head</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Sennheiser Momentum 4 vs Anker Soundcore Q30</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">These headphones sit in different price tiers. Momentum 4 adds aptX Adaptive support and a longer advertised battery life; Soundcore Q30 keeps the core wireless ANC feature set at a lower cost. The right choice depends on which differences your devices and listening habits can use.</p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <table class="cmp">
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Sennheiser Momentum 4</th><th>Anker Soundcore Q30</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td>Price tier</td><td>Premium; check current retailer price</td><td>Budget; check current retailer price</td></tr>
<tr><td>Noise cancellation</td><td>Adaptive hybrid ANC</td><td>Hybrid ANC with three modes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Codec advantage</td><td>aptX Adaptive on compatible devices</td><td>AAC and SBC</td></tr>
<tr><td>Battery (ANC on)</td><td>60 hours</td><td>40 hours</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bluetooth codecs</td><td>aptX Adaptive, aptX, AAC, SBC</td><td>AAC, SBC</td></tr>
<tr><td>Multipoint</td><td>Yes (2 devices)</td><td>Yes (2 devices)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wired mode</td><td>3.5mm cable included</td><td>3.5mm cable included</td></tr>
<tr><td>Companion app</td><td>Sennheiser Smart Control</td><td>Soundcore app</td></tr>
<tr><td>Published weight</td><td>293g</td><td>260g</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Sennheiser Momentum 4 wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Sennheiser Momentum 4 if...</h2>
    <p>You use a compatible device that supports aptX Adaptive and want that codec option.</p><p>You value the longer published battery rating: Sennheiser lists up to 60 hours, while Soundcore lists up to 40 hours with ANC enabled. Real runtime varies with volume, codec, calls, and ANC settings.</p><p>You are comfortable paying more for Momentum 4's feature set after checking current prices and return terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Anker Soundcore Q30 wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Anker Soundcore Q30 if...</h2>
    <p>You want hybrid ANC, app EQ, multipoint Bluetooth, and long battery life without entering the premium tier.</p><p>You prefer the lighter published weight or want a lower-cost pair for commuting and occasional travel.</p><p>You do not have a device that can use Momentum 4's aptX Adaptive support, reducing the value of that particular upgrade.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">The verdict</p>
    <p>Choose Momentum 4 when its longer published battery rating and aptX Adaptive support justify the premium for your devices. Choose Soundcore Q30 when you want the core ANC, app, and multipoint features at a lower price.</p><p>For either option, check microphone samples from a source you trust if call quality is your top priority; room noise and voice characteristics affect those comparisons.</p>
  </section>

